     "page": 1,
     "text": "Johnson LLC Clinic \nRe: Benjamin Horton (DOB 04/26/1985)\n\nDecember 03, 2024 \nToday, Mr. Horton visited for a follow-up regarding his peripheral neuropathy (idiopathic). The patient reports that his symptoms remain stable, with no significant changes in the pain or numbness experiences in his extremities. His blood pressure at this visit was 129/67, and he weighed 168 pounds. His current medication, duloxetine 30 mg, is effectively managing his symptoms, and he remains in a controlled status.\n\nJanuary 02, 2024 \nMr. Horton came in for a lab review today. His blood pressure was 125/77, and his weight was 182 pounds. He continues to deal with peripheral neuropathy (idiopathic) but reports no changes in his condition. His duloxetine has been working well for him, and he hasn't reported any side effects. The lab results from Heritage Diagnostic Services dated April 14, 2014, were also reviewed during this visit. The cholesterol/HDL ratio was 202/68, fructosamine level was 251, metabolite was negative, and gamma-GT was 51.\n\nJanuary 31, 2023 \nMr. Horton visited on this date due to a back strain. He has since recovered and is doing well. His blood pressure was 126/67, and he weighed 167 pounds. did not report any ongoing issues with his peripheral neuropathy (idiopathic).\n\nMarch 01, 2022 \nMr. Horton was seen for follow-up on his peripheral neuropathy (idiopathic). His blood pressure at this visit was 126/75, and he weighed 182 pounds. He continues to take duloxetine 30 which has been effective in managing his symptoms.\n\nSocial history: Mr. Horton is a former cigarette smoker who smoked about half a pack per day and quit in February 2011. There is no current use of alcohol or substances reported.\n\nFamily history: His brother has coronary artery disease, diagnosed at age 63, and his mother has had a myocardial infarction at age 78, both of whom are still living.\n\nGeneral physical examination: Horton alert, oriented, and in no acute distress. His cardiovascular, respiratory, and abdominal examinations are within normal limits. Neurological examination reveals diminished sensation in the lower consistent with peripheral neuropathy.\n\nMr. Horton will continue to be monitored for any changes in his condition, and his medication regimen will adjusted as necessary.\n\nDr. Jessica Adams \nNeurology \nJohnson LLC Clinic\n"
